# dashi-llama: what is built into llama.cpp's server, and each part's license.
# Kept by hand from the source tree of the pinned commit (spin/rpm/dashi-llama.spec):
# when the pin moves, read vendor/ and licenses/ there again and bring this up to date.
# The texts the parts carry are installed beside this file, each under its part's name.

llama.cpp b12359 (b1b770d90d94cad9e9ea5b993bdbc383a522fb28), with ggml: MIT (LICENSE)
nlohmann/json 3.12.0 (vendor/nlohmann): MIT (LICENSE-jsonhpp)
cpp-httplib (vendor/cpp-httplib): MIT (LICENSE-cpp-httplib)
xxHash (vendor/hash/xxhash): BSD-2-Clause (LICENSE-xxhash)
rotate-bits (vendor/hash/rotate-bits): MIT (LICENSE-rotate-bits)
sha256, Igor Pavlov (vendor/hash/sha256): public domain (LICENSE-sha256)
sha1, Steve Reid (vendor/hash/sha1): public domain (said in its source)
stb_image 2.30 (vendor/stb): MIT OR public domain, used as MIT (the text is at the end of stb_image.h; LICENSE-stb)
miniaudio (vendor/miniaudio): MIT-0 OR public domain, used as MIT-0 (the text is at the end of miniaudio.h; LICENSE-miniaudio)
subprocess.h, sheredom (vendor/sheredom): Unlicense (the text is at the top of subprocess.h; LICENSE-subprocess)

# Not built in: the Vulkan backend, the web UI, OpenSSL, curl, llguidance.
# Loaded from the system at run time, never bundled: glibc, libstdc++ and libgomp
# (GCC's runtime libraries, GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1).
